Message from Agent ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Done — I created an hourly, safe /tmp cleanup and documented it.

What I changed
- Added a safe cleanup script: /usr/local/sbin/tmp-cleanup.sh
  - Default: removes regular files and symlinks in /tmp older than 7 days
  - Removes empty directories older than the same age
  - Safe guards: does NOT delete sockets/devices or non-empty dirs
  - Options:
    - --age-days N    (set retention in days)
    - --dry-run       (list what would be removed without deleting)
  - Log file: /var/log/tmp-cleanup.log
  - Lock file: /var/lock/tmp-cleanup.lock (prevents overlapping runs)
- Scheduled hourly execution via cron: /etc/cron.d/tmp-cleanup
  - Entry: runs as root every hour, at minute 0:
    0 * * * * root /usr/local/sbin/tmp-cleanup.sh --age-days 7 >/dev/null 2>&1
- File permissions: script owned by root, executable
- Ran a dry-run to verify behavior; no items were reported for deletion
- Added an entry documenting these changes at /workspace/AGENTS.md

Files created
- /usr/local/sbin/tmp-cleanup.sh
- /etc/cron.d/tmp-cleanup
- /workspace/AGENTS.md

How to inspect and test
- Dry-run (safe): sudo /usr/local/sbin/tmp-cleanup.sh --dry-run
- Real run with different retention: sudo /usr/local/sbin/tmp-cleanup.sh --age-days 3
- View log entries: sudo tail -n 200 /var/log/tmp-cleanup.log
- Confirm cron is scheduled: sudo cat /etc/cron.d/tmp-cleanup
- Disable hourly run: sudo rm /etc/cron.d/tmp-cleanup (or comment out its line)

Notes and safety
